<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #070d1e; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">LEGAL COMPLIANCE</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Saharanpur Insured</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Transporting a motorcycle from Saharanpur requires a precise set of documents to satisfy both local regulations and the requirements of the Indian Bike Association (IBA). Presenting a complete, correctly formatted paperwork package not only speeds up customs clearance but also protects the owner against disputes, delays, or penalties.</p>
<p>Below is a concise checklist of the essential items that must accompany every bike shipment, along with brief notes on why each is mandatory.</p>

<p>Before handing over the bike to the carrier, verify that the following documents are prepared, self‑attested where required, and organized in the order presented.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Self‑attested RC (Registration Certificate) photocopy:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">This proves legal ownership and provides the vehicle’s registration number, chassis details, and engine specifications. The copy must be signed by the owner and bear the original’s stamp to be accepted by transport agents and customs officials.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current PUC (Pollution Under Control) certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A valid PUC, dated within the last three months, confirms that the bike meets emission standards. It is essential for interstate movement and is often inspected at loading bays and border checkpoints.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid insurance certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The policy should be active for the entire transit period and list the bike’s registration number. It safeguards the owner against accidental damage, theft, or third‑party liability while the vehicle is in transit.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑approved consignment bilty:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">This is the official freight document issued by the carrier, stamped and signed by an IBA representative. It records the consignor, consignee, vehicle details, and agreed freight charges, serving as the primary proof of shipment.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">In addition to the above, a <strong>100 % declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong> is strongly recommended.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This coverage insures the bike for its full market value against loss, total damage, or theft during sea or inland waterway transport.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The policy should explicitly state “100 % declared value” and be endorsed by the insurer, ensuring that the owner receives full reimbursement without depreciation deductions.</span></li></ul>

<p>Finally, double‑check that all documents are legible, signed, and dated correctly. Keep original copies for personal records and provide the carrier with clear, organized photocopies. Promptly addressing any missing or mismatched paperwork will prevent costly hold‑ups at checkpoints and guarantee a smooth, hassle‑free relocation of your bike from Saharanpur to its destination.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Saharanpur</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its destination, a systematic handover ensures that the vehicle is delivered in the same condition as it left the origin point, and that all contractual obligations are satisfied.</p>

<p>The handover process is divided into three core actions: a daylight condition re‑inspection, odometer verification against the LR (Logistics Receipt) bilty, and a signed condition sign‑off. Each action is documented and cross‑checked to protect both the logistics provider and the customer.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Daylight condition re‑inspection against pickup photos</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Conduct the inspection in natural daylight to reveal any surface damage, scratches, dents, or paint discrepancies that artificial lighting might conceal.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Retrieve the original pickup photographs from the dispatch system; these images should include multiple angles – front, rear, both sides, and close‑up of the instrument cluster.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare each current visual observation with the corresponding pickup photo, noting any new blemishes or confirming the absence of change.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Record findings on the handover checklist, attaching a timestamped photo of any newly identified defect for future reference.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Odometer verification against the LR bilty</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Read the odometer reading on the vehicle’s dashboard and write it down verbatim, including any decimal fractions if displayed.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Open the LR bilty (Logistics Receipt) which contains the recorded mileage at the time of pickup.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare the two figures; the difference should fall within the agreed‑upon mileage allowance or be justified by documented route deviations.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If a discrepancy exceeds the allowable variance, flag the entry, obtain a driver’s explanation, and update the bilty with an annotation.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signed condition sign‑off</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Present the completed inspection checklist, photographic evidence, and odometer comparison to the recipient.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Both the delivery agent and the recipient sign the document, confirming that the vehicle’s condition matches the recorded data.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Provide the recipient with a copy of the signed handover form and retain the original in the shipment file for audit purposes.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Upload the scanned or photographed copy to the central logistics portal to close the transaction.</span></li>
    </ul></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



